<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haut-Rhin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haut-Rhin is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> covering southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colmar">Colmar</a> as its prefecture and Mulhouse as its largest city. Created in 1790, it was annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> with the rest of Alsace from 1871 to 1918, apart from the Territoire de Belfort, which remained French. Since 2021 it has formed part of the European Collectivity of Alsace together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bas-rhin">Bas-Rhin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haut-rhin.jpg" alt="Haut-Rhin" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sanseiya · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colmar_Prefecture.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
